menu "F*CK module SDK"

    config FCK_AO_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the module's owner (0: KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH)"
        range 0 24
        default 0
        help
            The QP/C priority of the Active Object that owns the F*CK
            module, which is also its task's FreeRTOS priority. 0 takes
            kode-sdk's KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH; fck_ao.c says why. Level 3 is
            kode-sdk's own and is refused. Two Active Objects at one level
            are refused too (the start answers KODE_EXISTS), so an app whose
            own Active Object needs KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH moves this one to a
            level nothing in its image holds. With CONFIG_KODE_SCHEDULER
            there is no KODE_PRIO_USER_HIGH: set a level here.

    config FCK_SIG_OFFSET
        int "First signal of the F*CK SDK, above kode-sdk's MAX_SIG"
        range 1000 60000
        default 1300
        help
            fck_sys.h posts every signal to the Active Object it concerns, and an Active
            Object of the app cannot publish, so they live in a range of their own: MAX_SIG +
            this value, 90 numbers for what an app sees and 10 after them for the owner. The
            default sits beside the other module SDKs' (Mesh 1000, Robotics 1100, Camera
            1200). An app's own signals are MAX_SIG to MAX_SIG + 999; an app that also uses
            another module SDK keeps their ranges apart.

endmenu
